    ("cpr-adult", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should a single rescuer use for adult CPR?", "30:2", ('15:2 always', '5:1', 'Continuous compressions with no breaths ever for all cases'), "30:2 is standard for adult BLS. 15:2 always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should two rescuers use during adult BLS CPR?", "30:2", ('15:2 for adults always in BLS', '10:1', '3:1 only'), "Teams still use 30:2 in basic adult BLS. 15:2 for adults always in BLS is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "When checking for a pulse during adult CPR, how long should compressions be paused at most?", "As short as possible, under about 10 seconds for pulse checks", ('Over 1 minute routinely', 'Only compress every 5 minutes', 'Stop until AED arrives without compressing'), "Pauses reduce perfusion pressure. Over 1 minute routinely is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "An unresponsive adult is not breathing normally after you activate emergency response. What should you do first if you are trained in BLS?", "Start CPR beginning with compressions for trained lay rescuers in many programs", ('Wait for spontaneous recovery indefinitely', 'Only give breaths without compressions always', 'Leave to find help without activating EMS'), "Activate emergency response and use AED if available. Wait for spontaneous recovery indefinitely is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "Where should the heel of the hand be placed for adult chest compressions?", "Heel of hand on lower half of sternum", ('Xiphoid process directly', 'Upper abdomen', 'Left nipple only'), "Avoid compressing over xiphoid tip. Xiphoid process directly is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "What does full chest recoil mean during high-quality CPR?", "Allow chest to return fully without leaning on chest", ('Keep partial pressure always', 'Remove hands 6 inches away', 'Compress without release'), "Recoil allows heart filling. Keep partial pressure always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
