    ("cpr-adult", "How can rescuers reduce fatigue and maintain compression quality during prolonged CPR?", "Switch compressors every 2 minutes or sooner if quality drops", ('One person compresses 30 minutes straight without swap', 'Use only finger compressions', 'Stop for long breaks'), "Rotate to maintain depth and rate. One person compresses 30 minutes straight without swap is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "An unresponsive adult has only agonal gasps. How should you interpret this breathing pattern?", "Are not normal breathing; start CPR if no normal breathing", ('Mean patient is fine alone', 'Require only oxygen mask without compressions always', 'Rule out cardiac arrest'), "Agonal respirations may occur in early arrest. Mean patient is fine alone is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "When an AED arrives while you are performing adult CPR, what is the best sequence of actions?", "Apply pads and follow prompts with minimal compression pause", ('Stop CPR permanently before attaching pads', 'Use AED only after 30 minutes compressions', 'Place pads on wet chest without drying'), "Early defibrillation improves shockable rhythm outcomes. Stop CPR permanently before attaching pads is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-adult", "If you suspect opioid overdose in an unresponsive adult, what BLS actions are appropriate while EMS is activated?", "Provide ventilation support and naloxone per protocol while activating EMS", ('Withhold all breathing assistance', 'Only perform compressions if pulse present always without ventilation assessment', 'Delay EMS for hours'), "Respiratory depression may need ventilations and antidote. Withhold all breathing assistance is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
