    ("cpr-child", "For AHA pediatric BLS, which patients are generally managed with child rather than adult guidelines?", "Puberty not yet reached through about 1 year depending on size", ('All adults over 18 only', 'Only newborns under 1 hour', 'Only teenagers'), "Use child guidelines for pediatric victims not yet adult size. All adults over 18 only is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should a lone rescuer use for child CPR?", "30:2", ('15:2 only always for child always in all BLS without exception', '5:1', 'No ventilations ever'), "30:2 for single rescuer child BLS. 15:2 only always for child always in all BLS without... is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should two rescuers use for child CPR?", "15:2", ('30:2 always for two rescuers child', '10:1', 'Continuous compressions only always'), "Two rescuers use 15:2 in child BLS. 30:2 always for two rescuers child is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "What chest compression depth target is appropriate for a child during CPR?", "One third anterior-posterior diameter of chest or about 2 inches (5 cm)", ('Half inch only', '4 inches in all infants', 'Maximal possible always'), "Depth scales to child size. Half inch only is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "What compression rate should be used during child CPR?", "100 to 120 per minute", ('80 per minute only', '200 per minute', '40 per minute'), "Same rate target as adult high-quality CPR. 80 per minute only is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
    ("cpr-child", "A lone rescuer finds an unresponsive child who is not breathing normally after EMS activation. What should the rescuer do next?", "Start CPR with compressions if no normal breathing", ('Wait 10 minutes', 'Only slap back', 'Search for toys first'), "Begin CPR while help is coming if alone. Wait 10 minutes is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "When two rescuers are present for child cardiac arrest, how should roles and ratios be organized?", "One compresses, one ventilates with 15:2 after AED/EMS activation", ('Both leave patient', 'Only one watches phone', 'Alternate only breaths without compressions'), "Team roles improve quality. Both leave patient is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "Which maneuver should be used to open the airway for child CPR when trauma is not suspected?", "Head tilt-chin lift unless trauma suspected", ('Jaw thrust never in any case', 'Hyperextend neck always', 'Finger sweep blind always first'), "Trauma may require jaw thrust without head tilt. Jaw thrust never in any case is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
