    ("cpr-child", "Where and for how long should you check for a pulse in a child during BLS?", "Carotid or femoral for no more than 10 seconds", ('Radial only always in arrest', 'Never check pulse', 'Apical for 2 minutes pausing CPR'), "Quick check minimizes interruption. Radial only always in arrest is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "If a child is unresponsive with no pulse and a foreign body may be present, how does BLS integrate airway management?", "Start CPR; check mouth for visible object before breaths", ('Blind finger sweeps repeatedly', 'Heimlich only without CPR if pulseless', 'Ignore airway'), "Integrate airway check with CPR cycles. Blind finger sweeps repeatedly is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "Is compression-only CPR recommended for lay rescuers who can provide ventilations to a child in arrest?", "Is not recommended for lay rescuers who can provide breaths", ('Preferred over 30:2 always', 'Only for infants never child', 'Mandatory in all cases'), "Children often have respiratory causes of arrest. Preferred over 30:2 always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-child", "After ROSC in a child, what positioning and monitoring are appropriate?", "Support airway and monitor breathing unless trauma contraindicates", ('Head down only always', 'Standing immediately', 'Unmonitored waiting room'), "Continue oxygenation and evaluation. Head down only always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
