    ("cpr-infant", "What compression rate should rescuers use during infant CPR?", "100 to 120 per minute", ('60 per minute', '150 to 200 always required', '30 per minute'), "Same rate standard as other ages. 60 per minute is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should two rescuers use during infant BLS?", "15:2", ('30:2 always for two rescuers infant in BLS', '5:1 only', 'Breaths only'), "Two rescuers use 15:2 for infants. 30:2 always for two rescuers infant in BLS is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "What compression-to-ventilation ratio should a lone rescuer use during infant CPR?", "30:2", ('15:2 only', '10:1', 'Continuous compressions only always'), "Lone rescuer uses 30:2. 15:2 only is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "How should ventilations be given to an infant during CPR?", "Cover mouth and nose with rescuer mouth or barrier device making chest rise", ('Mouth only excluding nose always', 'Nose only always large volume', 'Cheek puff without chest rise OK'), "Seal includes mouth and nose. Mouth only excluding nose always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "If an infant is unresponsive and not breathing normally, when should CPR cycles begin relative to activating help?", "Give 2 rescue breaths after 30 compressions in 30:2 cycles after activating help", ('Wait for cyanosis only', 'Shake vigorously', 'Skip EMS if parent present'), "Start CPR after assessing responsiveness and breathing. Wait for cyanosis only is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "How should AED pads be applied to an infant when an AED is needed?", "Use pediatric system if available; follow manual if placing adult pads", ('Never be used under 1 year in any situation without reading device guidance', 'Both pads on chest stacked always without guidance', 'On legs only always'), "Minimize pause in compressions when attaching. Never be used under 1 year in any situation without... is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "How should you manage a choking infant who becomes unresponsive?", "Start CPR and look for object in mouth before breaths", ('Only back slaps forever without CPR if pulseless', 'Blind finger sweeps first always', 'Ignore until blue'), "CPR may dislodge object; visible objects may be removed. Only back slaps forever without CPR if pulseless is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "Why might you cover an infant during CPR in a cool environment?", "Prevent heat loss when environment is cool", ('Overheat infant always', 'Replace ventilation', 'Leave the infant uncovered in a cold room to speed cooling'), "Neonates lose heat quickly. Overheat infant always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "What is required for adequate chest recoil during infant compressions?", "Full chest return without resting weight on chest", ('Lean on chest between compressions', 'Lift hands 12 inches', 'Use bouncing motion'), "Recoil supports coronary filling. Lean on chest between compressions is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: High-Quality CPR — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/high-quality-cpr',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "What should a lone rescuer do about EMS activation when caring for an unresponsive infant?", "Perform CPR about 2 minutes before leaving to activate EMS if alone without phone", ('Never call 911', 'Leave immediately without CPR always', 'Only text friends'), "If phone present, activate speakerphone EMS while starting CPR. Never call 911 is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-infant", "After ROSC in an infant, what ongoing care is needed?", "Monitor breathing and pulse closely; keep warm", ('Feed immediately while unresponsive', 'Discharge without EMS', 'Place prone unobserved'), "Continued monitoring detects re-arrest. Feed immediately while unresponsive is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "When you first obtain an AED during resuscitation, what is the correct first step?", "Turn device on and follow voice prompts", ('Analyze before powering on', 'Remove all clothing including dry chest if not needed excessively', 'Place on patient thigh'), "Early AED use improves survival. Analyze before powering on is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "Where should AED pads be placed on a bare, dry chest?", "Bare dry chest per diagram (upper right and lower left typical)", ('Over medication patches without removal check', 'On wet skin without drying', 'Back only always'), "Remove transdermal patches if interfering per guidance. Over medication patches without removal check is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "What must rescuers do before the AED delivers a shock?", "Clear contact with patient and surface", ('Hold patient hand for support', 'Continue compressions through shock always', 'Stand on wet floor pooled without care'), "Clear ensures safety. Hold patient hand for support is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "If the AED advises that no shock is indicated, what should the team do immediately?", "Resume CPR immediately", ('Remove pads and leave', 'Wait without compressions', 'Only check blood pressure cuff'), "Non-shockable rhythms need compressions and epinephrine in ACLS. Remove pads and leave is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
