    ("cpr-aed", "Which special situations require adjustments before AED pad placement?", "Remove medication patch, dry chest, avoid placing pad over implanted pacemaker when possible", ('Ignore implanted devices always without adjustment', 'Use on conscious patient routinely', 'Place both pads on pacemaker generator deliberately'), "Adjust pad placement per training. Ignore implanted devices always without adjustment is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "How is pediatric AED energy delivered when pediatric equipment is available?", "Pediatric pads or attenuator when available", ('Adult pads on infant chest always without guidance', 'Lower battery setting manually unauthorized', 'No difference ever'), "Follow manufacturer pediatric instructions. Adult pads on infant chest always without guidance is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "Immediately after the AED delivers a shock, what should rescuers do?", "Resume CPR starting with compressions without delay for rhythm check by rescuer", ('Wait 5 minutes idle', 'Only breathe without compressions 10 minutes', 'Remove AED immediately'), "Post-shock rhythm may need immediate compressions. Wait 5 minutes idle is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "What maintenance helps keep public-access AEDs ready for use?", "Checking battery and pad expiration per schedule", ('Never inspect device', 'Store without pads', 'Disable alarm always'), "Ready devices save time in arrest. Never inspect device is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "What should you do with a transdermal medication patch that lies under an AED pad site?", "Removed and area wiped if interfering with adhesion or delivery", ('Ignored if loose', 'Cut through with scissors into patient always without care', 'Moved without hand hygiene ever'), "Prevent interference with pad contact. Ignored if loose is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "What should you do if chest hair prevents AED pads from adhering?", "Press firmly; use razor if supplied in kit", ('Never shave', 'Use gel randomly not approved', 'Skip AED entirely'), "Good contact reduces transthoracic impedance. Never shave is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-aed", "How should you manage AED use when the patient is on a conductive metal surface?", "Insulate with dry padding if energy arc concern per training", ('Always unsafe never use AED', 'Increase voltage manually', 'Remove patient delay 30 minutes'), "Minimize conductive paths. Always unsafe never use AED is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "How can you recognize mild choking in a responsive adult?", "Effective cough and some air movement", ('Silent inability to speak with cyanosis', 'Unconscious immediately always', 'No distress ever'), "Encourage forceful coughing if effective. Silent inability to speak with cyanosis is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "What is the initial treatment for severe choking in a responsive adult?", "Abdominal thrusts (Heimlich) until object out or unresponsive", ('Blind finger sweep in mouth always first', 'Back blows only never alternating per current BLS sequences', 'Wait until unconscious'), "Alternate 5 back blows and 5 abdominal thrusts in BLS. Blind finger sweep in mouth always first is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "What should you do if a choking adult becomes unresponsive?", "Lower to ground, activate EMS, begin CPR, check mouth for visible object", ('Heimlich only forever without CPR', 'Ignore airway', 'Shake only'), "Start CPR; look in mouth before breaths each cycle. Heimlich only forever without CPR is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "When should chest thrusts be used instead of abdominal thrusts for a choking victim?", "Chest thrusts instead of abdominal thrusts", ('No assistance ever', 'Only water drinking', 'Finger sweep blind'), "Chest thrusts reduce abdominal injury risk. No assistance ever is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "How should you treat a responsive infant with severe airway obstruction?", "5 back slaps and 5 chest thrusts alternating", ('Abdominal Heimlich always', 'Only finger sweeps', 'Ignore until blue'), "Support head and neck during maneuvers. Abdominal Heimlich always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "What should you do if a choking infant becomes unresponsive?", "Start CPR; check mouth for object before breaths", ('Only back slaps indefinitely', 'Hold upside down shaking', 'Skip EMS'), "CPR cycles integrate airway checks. Only back slaps indefinitely is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "After an episode of severe choking resolves, why should the patient be evaluated medically?", "Encourage medical evaluation if severe episode or complications", ('Send home without assessment always', 'Ignore sore throat', 'Discharge while hypoxic'), "Complications include swelling or aspiration. Send home without assessment always is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
    ("cpr-choking", "How should severe choking be managed in a conscious child?", "Back blows and abdominal thrusts per size-appropriate BLS", ('Only adult Heimlich always on toddler without modification', 'Wait for coughing to fail hours', 'Slap face only'), "Use pediatric modifications. Only adult Heimlich always on toddler without modifi... is incorrect here because it would not provide effective BLS care in this scenario.", ('American Heart Association: Adult Basic Life Support Guidelines — https://cpr.heart.org/en/resuscitation-science/cpr-and-ecc-guidelines/adult-basic-life-support',)),
